  "title": "An elementary obstruction to same-ground-set matroid-rank approximation",
  "description": "<p>A credited self-contained elementary exposition of the source-displayed symmetric ordinary unscaled same-ground-set matroid-rank approximation question. Inputs are nonnegative monotone submodular functions with zero empty-set value and every singleton value one. The conventional meaning of constant is taken to be dimension-independent; V\u00e9gh's complete source contribution does not separately print an all-ground-sets quantifier. Both r(S)/alpha &lt;= f(S) &lt;= alpha*r(S) comparisons are retained.</p><p>The classical square-root-cardinality input on n elements forces alpha &gt;= n^(1/6). Its exact optimum among all matroids is min over integer 1&lt;=R&lt;=n of max(sqrt(R),sqrt(n)/R), attained by uniform ranks. On m^2 elements the rational cardinality input g(empty)=0 and g(nonempty)=1+(|S|-1)/m forces alpha^2+alpha &gt;= m and alpha &gt;= n^(1/4)/sqrt(2). Sharpness is only for the square-root family. Full quantified proofs and empty, singleton, loop and m=1 boundaries are included.</p><p>Credits: DDSSS 2013 Appendix D Lemma D.1 for prior uniform-rank decomposition, with corrected direct difference coefficients; classical concave-cardinality submodularity attributed by Balcan-Harvey to Lov\u00e1sz 1983 (original body unread); GHIM actual root-linear output and query-hard rank-input distinction; Schrijver Section 44.6b, credited there to Helgason, for expanded copied-element representation, distinct from one ordinary rank on original V (Helgason original unread). The input families and their rank-sum structure are classical. Exact one-rank argument and generic-envelope historical attribution are unresolved in the bounded review. No new-function, new-representation, firstness, intellectual-priority, independently evidenced discovery, exhaustive literature or current-worldwide-open-status claim is made. Other unread citation-chain consequences remain unknown.</p><p>Version 1.0, dated 14 October 2026. Alec Kriebel, ORCID 0009-0001-9320-500X, independent researcher, sole named author. Extensive AI assistance in solving, mathematical verification, source comparison, coding and writing. UNREFEREED: no human review, journal acceptance or formal certification. Authored exposition and code: CC BY 4.0. The supportkit preserves all nine original bodies and selected authored stage reports, checkers, output streams, pins and receipts; stage-specific AI audits and frozen inputs are identified in REVIEW_HISTORY.json and evidence/INDEX.md. The original edition had no executable; a portable adaptation of the newly authored audit checker was actually run for preparation, with no omitted historical-code replay. Finite checks supplement the written infinite proof. No third-party full bodies, extracts, images or raw/private/environment caches are redistributed. These files describe a dated local preparation stage and are not a deposit/publication record.</p>",
